node_modules/
dist/

# The real environment file, never committed: it holds a database
# password.
.env
.env.local

# ...but the EXAMPLE is documentation and must be committed. The
# repository root ignores `.env*`, which sweeps it up too, so it is
# explicitly un-ignored here. Without this line a new developer
# clones the project and has nothing telling them the variable is
# ERP_DATABASE_URL rather than DATABASE_URL — which is the one
# thing about this setup they must not guess at.
!.env.example
